// 장소 영어 번역(이름, 작품, 위치, 설명). 한국어 원본은 spots.js 에 있습니다. 번역이 없는 항목은 한국어로 표시됩니다.
window.SPOTS_EN = {
1:{name:"Kamakurakokomae Station Crossing",work:"Slam Dunk",loc:"Kamakura, Kanagawa, Japan",desc:"Right next to the station is the very railroad crossing where the Enoden tram ran along the sea in the opening of the Slam Dunk TV anime.\nBeyond the crossing you can see the Shonan coast and the horizon, and fans and tourists still gather all day to recreate scenes from the series.\nThe most popular shot is the green-and-cream Enoden train passing by; for safety, please stay on the roadside when taking photos."},
2:{name:"Suga Shrine Stairs",work:"Your Name.",loc:"Shinjuku, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"This is where, in the final scene, the grown-up Taki and Mitsuha recognize each other from the top and bottom of a staircase and ask, \"What's your name?\"\nThe stairs rising between narrow residential streets and the small shrine grounds form a picture-perfect composition, and since the film's release it has become a leading pilgrimage site for fans around the world.\nThe surroundings are an ordinary residential area, so it is polite to take photos quietly and leave; ema (wish plaques) left by fans hang in the shrine grounds."},
3:{name:"Hallstatt Village",work:"Frozen",loc:"Salzkammergut, Austria",desc:"With pastel wooden houses stacked up the cliffs beside the lake, this village is often mentioned as one of the candidate inspirations for the kingdom of Arendelle.\nThe clear Lake Hallstatt, the slopes of the Dachstein, and a pointed church spire come together in a fairy-tale scene.\nIt is a UNESCO World Heritage area that is beautiful in every season, and in winter its snow-covered look comes closest to the mood of the film."},
4:{name:"Colmar Old Town",work:"Howl's Moving Castle",loc:"Colmar, Alsace, France",desc:"It is said that the Alsatian towns director Hayao Miyazaki saw on a research trip were a major inspiration for the streets of Sophie's town in Howl's Moving Castle.\nColorful half-timbered houses, flower-decked windows, and the canal-side \"Little Venice\" quarter resemble the streets in the film.\nIn the Christmas season markets open and the whole town becomes even more fairy-tale-like, drawing many travelers."},
5:{name:"Dogo Onsen Honkan",work:"Spirited Away",loc:"Matsuyama, Ehime, Japan",desc:"One of Japan's oldest hot springs, its three-story wooden main building is often cited as the model for the bathhouse \"Aburaya\" in Spirited Away.\nThough not officially confirmed, the complex roofs, winding corridors, and the glow of its lights at night echo the film's mood and have made it a pilgrimage spot for fans.\nIt is also the setting of the novel \"Botchan,\" and you can actually bathe and tour the building's interior, making it a good place to experience the world of the work."},
6:{name:"Marrakech Medina",work:"Aladdin",loc:"Marrakech, Morocco",desc:"Agrabah in Aladdin is a fictional city, but the atmosphere of an Arab city with narrow alleys and tangled markets can be felt in a medina like Marrakech.\nInside the red walls, souks selling spices, textiles, and metalwork stretch like a maze, and the central square Jemaa el-Fnaa is packed with street performers every night.\nIt is a UNESCO World Heritage site where you can enjoy walking the alleys and imagining Aladdin leaping across rooftops."},
7:{name:"Serengeti National Park",work:"The Lion King",loc:"Serengeti, Tanzania",desc:"The Lion King team did on-site research on the African savanna to capture animal movement and scenery, and the Serengeti is the place that best represents those images.\nEndless grasslands, acacia trees, and the \"Great Migration\" of millions of wildebeest and zebras resemble the grand scenes of the film.\nA safari tour against a horizon that turns red at sunset lets you feel the emotion of the film's opening in real life."},
8:{name:"Mont Saint-Michel",work:"Tangled",loc:"Normandy, France",desc:"The island abbey rising out of the sea is known to have inspired the castle and town design of the kingdom in Disney's Tangled.\nThe tidal range is very large, so the island is cut off at high tide and a path opens across the mudflats at low tide, creating a unique landscape.\nClimb the narrow stepped alleys to the abbey at the top and you can look out over the entire Normandy coast; it is a UNESCO World Heritage site."},
9:{name:"Angel Falls",work:"Up",loc:"Canaima National Park, Venezuela",desc:"The Pixar team explored Venezuela's tepuis (table-top mountains) in person, and Angel Falls became an important source of inspiration for \"Paradise Falls\" in the film.\nWith a drop of 979 m it is the world's highest waterfall, and the sight of its stream dispersing into mist before reaching the bottom is striking.\nIt lies deep in a hard-to-reach jungle and requires a boat and trekking, but that is exactly what lets you feel like you are on Carl's adventure."},
10:{name:"Notre-Dame Cathedral",work:"The Hunchback of Notre Dame",loc:"Paris, France",desc:"Disney's The Hunchback of Notre Dame, based on Victor Hugo's novel, makes this cathedral and its bell tower the central stage of the story.\nThe bell tower where Quasimodo looked down over Paris, the gargoyles, and the splendid rose window are hallmark elements of Gothic architecture.\nIt reopened after restoration following the 2019 fire, and even just seeing the exterior from the Île de la Cité on the Seine lets you feel the atmosphere of the film."},
11:{name:"Visby Old Town",work:"Kiki's Delivery Service",loc:"Gotland, Sweden",desc:"It is said that after researching Stockholm and the island of Gotland in Sweden, director Miyazaki drew the port city of \"Koriko\" where Kiki settles.\nSurrounded by medieval walls, Visby is an old Northern European city where red roofs, cobblestone streets, and ruined churches draped in roses come together.\nIt is a UNESCO World Heritage site, and in summer a medieval festival is held that fills the town with energy like the town in the film."},
12:{name:"Eiffel Tower",work:"Miraculous: Tales of Ladybug & Cat Noir",loc:"Paris, France",desc:"The two heroes of the French animation Miraculous are active against a Parisian backdrop, and the Eiffel Tower is a symbolic stage that appears in almost every season.\nIts sparkling night lights and iron structure suit the wire action sweeping across the city.\nFrom the Trocadéro or the Champ de Mars you can photograph views similar to the compositions in the series."},
13:{name:"Shibuya Scramble Crossing",work:"Jujutsu Kaisen",loc:"Shibuya, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"The \"Shibuya Incident\" arc of Jujutsu Kaisen drew attention for depicting real streets such as Shibuya Station and Center Gai in great detail.\nKnown as the busiest pedestrian crossing in the world, it offers the spectacle of hundreds of people crossing at once each time the signal changes.\nLooking down from nearby observation decks and station walkways, you can recall the battle compositions of the series."},
14:{name:"Shirakawa-go Gassho Village",work:"Higurashi: When They Cry",loc:"Shirakawa, Gifu, Japan",desc:"The \"Hinamizawa village\" setting of Higurashi: When They Cry is well known to be modeled on Shirakawa-go.\nSteep thatched-roof gassho-style houses clustered between rice fields and mountains overlap with the quiet yet tense atmosphere of the work.\nThe village seen from the observation deck photographs especially well in snowy winter and lush green summer, and it is also a UNESCO World Heritage site."},
15:{name:"Chichibu Bridge and Chichibu City",work:"Anohana: The Flower We Saw That Day",loc:"Chichibu, Saitama, Japan",desc:"Known as the setting of \"Anohana,\" Chichibu became a leading pilgrimage city for fans after the series was released.\nThe Chichibu Bridge, the place used as the secret base, shrines, and streets overlap with scenes from the series, and walking routes with maps have been prepared.\nIt is reachable from Tokyo by train, and local shops and the tourist office actively provide merchandise and maps for the series."},
16:{name:"Shinjuku Gyoen",work:"The Garden of Words",loc:"Shinjuku, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"This is the park with the gazebo where the two protagonists meet on rainy days in Makoto Shinkai's \"The Garden of Words.\"\nEven in the middle of the city, Japanese, French, and English gardens blend together for quiet strolls.\nThe sound of rain in the rainy season, ripples spreading on the pond, and the pink scenery of cherry blossom season all resemble the delicate visuals of the film."},
17:{name:"Big Ben and the Palace of Westminster",work:"Peter Pan",loc:"London, United Kingdom",desc:"Big Ben appears in Disney's Peter Pan when Wendy and her brothers sprinkle fairy dust and fly up into the London sky.\nThe Gothic clock tower, the Thames, and Westminster Bridge come together as a view that represents Britain.\nAt dusk and at night the lights come on, creating an atmosphere similar to the night sky on the way to Neverland."},
18:{name:"Akihabara Electric Town",work:"Steins;Gate",loc:"Chiyoda, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"The sci-fi anime Steins;Gate uses Akihabara as its main stage and realistically depicts the Radio Kaikan and the streets.\nA center of otaku culture packed with electronics shops, game centers, and subculture stores, it draws many fans.\nWalking around to find the location of the Future Gadget Laboratory in the story or browsing related merchandise is a popular route."},
19:{name:"Neuschwanstein Castle",work:"Sleeping Beauty",loc:"Füssen, Bavaria, Germany",desc:"Built by King Ludwig II of Bavaria, this castle is famous for inspiring the castle in Disney's Sleeping Beauty and the design of the Disneyland castle.\nWith white limestone walls and pointed towers rising on a mountain, the scene blending with the foothills of the Alps looks like a fairy tale.\nThe view from Marienbrücke is the most famous photo spot, and it is a popular destination in every season."},
20:{name:"Lake Suwa",work:"Your Name.",loc:"Suwa, Nagano, Japan",desc:"The village of Itomori and its lake, the setting of Your Name., are widely known to be modeled on Lake Suwa in Nagano.\nA lake in the middle of a basin surrounded by mountains, with lakeside towns stretching along it, closely resembles the scenery of the film.\nThe walking paths around the lake, hot springs, and annual fireworks are local attractions, and pilgrimage fans visit often."},
21:{name:"Taj Mahal",work:"Aladdin",loc:"Agra, India",desc:"It is said that the white dome and symmetrical structure reminiscent of the Taj Mahal were used in the design of the Sultan's palace in Aladdin.\nA marble tomb built by the Mughal emperor Shah Jahan in memory of his queen, it changes color to pink and gold with the morning and sunset light.\nThe perfectly symmetrical composition reflected in the long pool shows the mysterious atmosphere of the palace in the film."},
22:{name:"Osaka Castle",work:"Detective Conan",loc:"Osaka, Osaka, Japan",desc:"Osaka Castle regularly appears as a setting in episodes and movies involving Osaka, where the western Japan detective Heiji Hattori is active.\nBuilt by Toyotomi Hideyoshi, the castle boasts a gold-leaf-decorated main keep, moats, and stone walls that look magnificent.\nThe surrounding Osaka Castle Park is a spot for cherry blossoms and autumn leaves, popular with Conan fans and general tourists alike."},
23:{name:"Ogaki City Waterways",work:"A Silent Voice",loc:"Ogaki, Gifu, Japan",desc:"Kyoto Animation's \"A Silent Voice\" takes Ogaki, Gifu as its main setting and realistically depicts its river, bridges, and streets.\nBecause of the bridge scene where Ishida and Nishimiya feed the carp, fans walk the waterways on a pilgrimage.\nKnown as a city of water with many clear channels, it is nice for walking, and the city hall's tourism office also provides a map of the work."},
24:{name:"Hakone",work:"Neon Genesis Evangelion",loc:"Hakone, Kanagawa, Japan",desc:"The fortress city \"Tokyo-3\" in Evangelion is set around the Hakone area, and Hakone place names are used in the series.\nLake Ashi, the Hakone Tozan Railway, and the volcanic terrain of Owakudani overlap with the setting of the Angel battles, drawing many fans.\nYou can also enjoy hot springs and views of Mount Fuji, making it a good area to combine an Evangelion pilgrimage with general sightseeing."},
25:{name:"Central Park",work:"Madagascar",loc:"New York, USA",desc:"DreamWorks' Madagascar is a story that begins when the animals of the Central Park Zoo leave New York.\nIn the middle of Manhattan, lakes, forests, and lawns spread out, offering an oasis-like view in contrast to the skyscrapers.\nWalking past the Central Park Zoo, Belvedere Castle, and the boat lake, you can recall the opening scenes of the film."},
26:{name:"Oarai Town",work:"Girls und Panzer",loc:"Oarai, Ibaraki, Japan",desc:"Girls und Panzer made the port town of Oarai in Ibaraki the stage of a school city built on a school ship, becoming a symbolic example of regional revitalization.\nCharacter panels from the series are set up around town, and the shopping streets and harbor scenery overlap with the work, making a pilgrimage easy.\nReal tanks appear at the annual \"Marine Battle\" event, and fans gather from all over the country."},
27:{name:"Fushimi Inari Taisha",work:"Inari, Konkon, Koi Iroha",loc:"Kyoto, Kyoto, Japan",desc:"This series, in which the heroine gains the power of the fox deity Inari, uses Fushimi Inari Shrine in Kyoto directly as its stage.\nThe \"Senbon Torii,\" a path of thousands of vermilion torii gates running along the mountain, creates a mysterious atmosphere both day and night.\nIt takes about two hours to reach the summit, and fox statues are everywhere, so it is fun to walk while comparing with the anime."},
28:{name:"Kauai Island",work:"Lilo & Stitch",loc:"Hawaii, USA",desc:"Lilo & Stitch is set on the Hawaiian island of Kauai and tells how the experiment Stitch, who came from space, becomes part of Lilo's family.\nGreen mountains, emerald seas, and the cliffs of the Nā Pali Coast fit well with the tropical island atmosphere of the film.\nYou can experience surfing, hiking, and hula culture, and feel the film's theme of \"ohana (family)\" in real life."},
29:{name:"Sydney Opera House",work:"Finding Nemo",loc:"Sydney, Australia",desc:"In Finding Nemo, Marlin and Dory cross the open sea toward Sydney Harbour, where the dentist's aquarium holding Nemo is located.\nThe Opera House, with its unique shell-like roofs, is a symbol of the city together with Sydney Harbour and the Harbour Bridge.\nViewed from a harbour ferry or the Botanic Garden lookout, you can recall the scenery of the film's final destination."},
30:{name:"Venice Canals",work:"ARIA The Animation",loc:"Venice, Italy",desc:"ARIA's \"Neo-Venezia\" is a water city recreated on Mars, but its scenery and culture are taken almost directly from Venice, Italy.\nSights such as narrow canals traveled by gondolas, stone bridges, and St. Mark's Square are depicted in the work as the streets of \"Aqua.\"\nRiding a gondola through the canals, you can feel the calm as if guided by an \"Undine\" gondolier from the series."},
31:{name:"Numazu Port",work:"Love Live! Sunshine!!",loc:"Numazu, Shizuoka, Japan",desc:"Uchiura, the setting of Love Live! Sunshine!!, is modeled on Numazu in Shizuoka.\nThe harbor, beaches, and observation spots with a view of Mount Fuji overlap with scenes from the series, drawing many fans.\nPosters and limited-edition menus of the series at downtown shops, buses, and restaurants have made it an established pilgrimage city."},
32:{name:"Tomonoura",work:"Ponyo",loc:"Fukuyama, Hiroshima, Japan",desc:"It is said that director Miyazaki stayed in Tomonoura and conceived Ponyo there.\nAn old port town on the Seto Inland Sea, it preserves its Edo-period look with a lighthouse-style lantern, stone seawalls, and narrow alleys.\nPonyo-related decorations and information boards around town make it easy to feel the seaside-town atmosphere of the film."},
33:{name:"Yakushima",work:"Princess Mononoke",loc:"Kagoshima, Japan",desc:"The mysterious forest of Princess Mononoke is said to have been greatly inspired by the moss forest of Shiratani Unsuikyo on Yakushima.\nThousand-year-old cedars such as Jomon Sugi, moss-covered rocks, and clear streams resemble the Forest Spirit's forest in the film.\nIt is a UNESCO World Heritage site, and because the island gets frequent rain, the forest feels even greener and more mysterious."},
34:{name:"Byodo-in",work:"Sound! Euphonium",loc:"Uji, Kyoto, Japan",desc:"Kyoto Animation's \"Sound! Euphonium\" is set in Uji, and Ujibashi Bridge and Byodo-in often appear in the series.\nThe Heian-period Phoenix Hall is also famous as the building on the 10-yen coin, and its reflection in the pond is beautiful.\nA walking course along the Uji River, where the characters walked, is popular with fans."},
35:{name:"Old Toyosato Elementary School",work:"K-On!",loc:"Toyosato, Shiga, Japan",desc:"The former Toyosato Elementary School, known as the model for Sakuragaoka High School in K-On!, is a modern building designed by William Merrell Vories.\nThe classrooms, corridors, and stairs resemble the music room scenes in the series, and many fans visit to tour the inside of the school.\nThe real school building is preserved as a cultural property, with character statues and souvenirs from the series."},
36:{name:"Nishinomiya",work:"The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya",loc:"Nishinomiya, Hyogo, Japan",desc:"The school and streets of The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya are modeled on Nishinomiya city.\nAreas around Koyoen Station, the Shukugawa riverside, and the high school overlap with scenes from the series, and fans walk the streets on a pilgrimage.\nLocated between Osaka and Kobe, it is easy to reach, and with many shrines and parks nearby it makes a good day trip."},
37:{name:"Guanajuato Old Town",work:"Coco",loc:"Guanajuato, Mexico",desc:"Pixar's Coco \"Land of the Dead\" is said to have drawn inspiration from the colorful buildings stacked up the slopes of Guanajuato.\nBlue, yellow, and pink houses fill the hillsides, and narrow alleys and underground tunnel roads create a unique cityscape.\nAround the Day of the Dead each autumn, the whole city is decorated, so you can feel the festive atmosphere of the film as it is."},
38:{name:"Dubrovnik Old Town",work:"Porco Rosso",loc:"Dubrovnik, Croatia",desc:"The Adriatic scenery of Porco Rosso is often compared to Croatian coastal cities, and Dubrovnik is a leading example.\nRed roofs and medieval walls blend with the blue sea, earning it the name \"Pearl of the Adriatic.\"\nWalking the full circuit of the walls gives views resembling the coast where Porco flew."},
39:{name:"Asakusa Senso-ji",work:"Demon Slayer",loc:"Taito, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"The scene where Tanjiro first meets Kibutsuji Muzan in Demon Slayer is set in the streets of Asakusa in the Taisho era.\nThe red Kaminarimon, the Nakamise shopping street, and the Senso-ji main hall show the scenery of Tokyo's oldest temple.\nRenting a kimono and walking around lets you feel the period atmosphere of the series even more vividly."},
40:{name:"Jiufen",work:"Spirited Away",loc:"New Taipei City, Taiwan",desc:"With red lanterns lighting up along its hillside streets, Jiufen is visited by many fans because it reminds people of the hot spring town in Spirited Away.\nStudio Ghibli has not officially acknowledged this place as the model, but its night views, stepped alleys, and teahouses resemble the work.\nIt is most beautiful when the red lanterns are lit after sunset, and street food and teahouses are popular too."},
41:{name:"Yokohama Minato Mirai",work:"Bungo Stray Dogs",loc:"Yokohama, Kanagawa, Japan",desc:"Bungo Stray Dogs is a supernatural-battle series set in Yokohama, and the harbor scenery and buildings are depicted realistically.\nThe Cosmo Clock 21 Ferris wheel, Landmark Tower, and red-brick warehouses overlap with scenes in the work.\nThe harbor night view is dazzling at night, and collaboration events and stamp rallies are held from time to time, which fans love."},
42:{name:"Tanegashima",work:"5 Centimeters per Second",loc:"Kagoshima, Japan",desc:"The third episode of Makoto Shinkai's 5 Centimeters per Second is set on Tanegashima in Kagoshima.\nThe rocket launch site, blue sea, and quiet coastal roads deepen the protagonist's lonely feelings.\nThe Tanegashima Space Center, the heart of Japan's space development, is also here, so you can enjoy rockets and the film's scenery together."},
43:{name:"Maienfeld Heidi Village",work:"Heidi, Girl of the Alps",loc:"Graubünden, Switzerland",desc:"This is the village known as the setting of the original novel Heidi and of the TV anime Heidi, Girl of the Alps.\nGreen meadows, vineyards, and snow-covered Alpine peaks go well with Heidi's pure story.\nThere are facilities such as Heidi Village and Heidi's hut, which are popular with families."},
44:{name:"Antwerp Cathedral of Our Lady",work:"A Dog of Flanders",loc:"Antwerp, Belgium",desc:"This cathedral is where Nello ends his life looking at Rubens' paintings in the final scene of A Dog of Flanders.\nRubens' \"The Elevation of the Cross\" and \"The Descent from the Cross\" actually hang in the church, so you can see the scene from the work in person.\nIn the square in front there is a memorial to Nello and Patrasche, and many Korean and Japanese fans visit."},
45:{name:"Tokyo Tower",work:"Magic Knight Rayearth",loc:"Minato, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"The opening of CLAMP's Magic Knight Rayearth, in which three girls are summoned to another world at Tokyo Tower, is famous.\nThe red-and-white steel tower, completed in 1958, is a symbol of Tokyo and often appears in other works such as Cardcaptor Sakura.\nBoth the view of Tokyo's night scenery from the observatory and the view looking up at the tower from the park below are popular photo spots."},
46:{name:"Odaiba",work:"Digimon Adventure",loc:"Koto, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"The Fuji TV headquarters building and the Rainbow Bridge in Odaiba appear as important settings in the Digimon Adventure movie and TV series.\nOn the artificial island of Odaiba there are many attractions, including shopping malls, a replica of the Statue of Liberty, and a life-size Gundam.\nDigimon fans can recall scenes from the series at the Fuji TV building observation deck and the seaside park."},
47:{name:"Ghibli Museum",work:"The world of Studio Ghibli",loc:"Mitaka, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"A museum where you can experience the world of Studio Ghibli, planned personally by director Hayao Miyazaki.\nInside are original drawings, the animation production process, the Catbus from Totoro, and a theater showing short Ghibli films.\nAdvance reservation tickets are required and photography inside is prohibited, so you need to take in the atmosphere with your eyes."},
48:{name:"Yuwaku Onsen",work:"Hanasaku Iroha",loc:"Kanazawa, Ishikawa, Japan",desc:"Hanasaku Iroha is set at the ryokan of the \"Kissuiso\" hot spring, modeled on Yuwaku Onsen in Ishikawa.\nThe narrow hot spring street, wooden ryokan, and small shrine overlap almost exactly with scenes from the work.\nThe annual \"Bonbori Festival\" includes events tied to the work, and fans come from all over the country."},
49:{name:"Kure, Hiroshima",work:"In This Corner of the World",loc:"Kure, Hiroshima, Japan",desc:"Director Sunao Katabuchi's film depicts everyday life in Hiroshima and Kure during wartime with great care.\nThe harbor and hillside town scenery of Kure were precisely recreated based on maps and photos from the period.\nAt the Kure Yamato Museum and the JMSDF Kure Museum you can also learn about the history of the military port city of that time."},
50:{name:"Washinomiya Shrine",work:"Lucky Star",loc:"Kuki, Saitama, Japan",desc:"Known as the origin of anime pilgrimage, this is the shrine on whose grounds the Hiiragi sisters' home is set in Lucky Star.\nAfter the series aired, fans came in great numbers and hung ema (wish plaques), and it became a leading example of revitalizing local commerce.\nEvents related to the work are held at the annual festival, showing a culture where the community and fans take part together."},
51:{name:"Cinque Terre",work:"Luca",loc:"Liguria, Italy",desc:"Pixar's Luca is set in the Portorosso village on the Italian Riviera, and the Cinque Terre area is said to have been a major inspiration.\nFive villages with pastel-colored houses clinging to cliffs in layers, set against the sea, resemble the scenery in the film.\nYou can enjoy the film's summer atmosphere along the coastal hiking trails and by traveling between the villages by train."},
52:{name:"Hida-Furukawa",work:"Your Name.",loc:"Hida, Gifu, Japan",desc:"The town, library, and train station that Taki visits in search of Mitsuha in Your Name. are modeled on Hida city.\nPlaces such as Hida-Furukawa Station, the city library, and the Shirakabe-dozo street resemble scenes from the film, and fans make pilgrimages.\nWhite-walled earthen storehouses and the Seto River canal with carp swimming give a quiet, old-town atmosphere."},
53:{name:"Lake Motosu",work:"Laid-Back Camp",loc:"Minobu, Yamanashi, Japan",desc:"Lake Motosu, one of the Fuji Five Lakes, appears as the place where the heroine first camps alone in Laid-Back Camp.\nThe view of Mount Fuji on the back of the 1,000-yen note is said to be from this lake, which makes it even more famous.\nMount Fuji sunrises and starry skies seen from the lakeside campground show exactly the \"laid-back camping\" mood that the series emphasizes."},
54:{name:"King's Cross Station Platform 9¾",work:"Harry Potter series",loc:"London, United Kingdom",desc:"Inside King's Cross Station there is a photo spot recreating the platform entrance where Harry went to board the Hogwarts Express.\nThere is always a line to take photos with a trolley half-embedded in the wall and a Hogwarts scarf flying in the wind.\nRight next to it is the official Harry Potter shop, where you can buy wands and souvenirs."},
55:{name:"Hobbiton Movie Set",work:"The Lord of the Rings / The Hobbit",loc:"Matamata, New Zealand",desc:"A permanently preserved tourist site where the Shire village set built by director Peter Jackson for The Lord of the Rings and The Hobbit stands.\n44 hobbit holes, the Party Tree, and the Green Dragon inn are recreated at full scale along green hills.\nAt the end of the guided tour you can enjoy a beer at the inn and soak in the atmosphere of the films."},
56:{name:"Joker Stairs",work:"Joker",loc:"The Bronx, New York, USA",desc:"The stairs where Arthur Fleck dances his way down in Joker are real, in the Highbridge area of the Bronx, New York.\nSince the film's release, tourists have flocked to recreate the poses, and the stairs are now nicknamed the \"Joker Stairs.\"\nThey are also part of residents' daily lives, so visitors should be careful about noise and litter."},
57:{name:"Griffith Observatory",work:"La La Land",loc:"Los Angeles, USA",desc:"This observatory is the setting of the scene where Sebastian and Mia float up and dance among the stars.\nIt sits on a hill overlooking downtown Los Angeles and the Hollywood Sign, and is famous for its night views.\nAdmission is free, and inside you can also enjoy planetarium shows and science exhibits."},
58:{name:"Panmunjom Joint Security Area",work:"Joint Security Area (JSA)",loc:"Paju, Gyeonggi, South Korea",desc:"Park Chan-wook's film Joint Security Area deals with a tragic story surrounding the military demarcation line at Panmunjom.\nReal places such as the blue conference buildings, the military demarcation line, and the Bridge of No Return were the models for the film's settings.\nGeneral tourists can visit only on pre-registered tours, and strict rules apply on site."},
59:{name:"Wadi Rum Desert",work:"Dune / The Martian",loc:"Wadi Rum, Jordan",desc:"With red sand and huge sandstone rocks, Wadi Rum was used as a filming location for Arrakis in Dune and Mars scenes in The Martian.\nIts unreal scenery, known as the \"Valley of the Moon,\" looks like an alien planet.\nThrough jeep tours, camel trekking, and desert camps you can experience the atmosphere of the films firsthand."},
60:{name:"Colosseum",work:"Gladiator",loc:"Rome, Italy",desc:"The arena where Maximus fights as a gladiator in Ridley Scott's Gladiator was recreated with the Colosseum as its model.\nCompleted around AD 80, this amphitheater could hold about 50,000 people, and its imposing outer walls and underground structures remain today.\nSome scenes in the film used CGI and a set in Malta, but visiting the real Colosseum gives you a similar sense of awe."},
61:{name:"Empire State Building",work:"King Kong",loc:"New York, USA",desc:"It remains in film history as the building the giant gorilla climbs to fight airplanes in the final scene of the 1933 classic King Kong.\nThis 102-story Art Deco skyscraper, completed in 1931, was for a long time the tallest building in the world.\nFrom the 86th and 102nd floor observatories you can see all of Manhattan and the Hudson River."},
62:{name:"Machu Picchu",work:"The Motorcycle Diaries",loc:"Cusco, Peru",desc:"Machu Picchu appears as an important scene in The Motorcycle Diaries, which depicts Che Guevara's youthful journey across South America.\nThe ruins of an Inca city on a mountaintop in the Andes at 2,430 m above sea level, it is a UNESCO World Heritage site.\nTerraced fields and temple ruins emerging from the morning mist convey the emotion of the film just as it is."},
63:{name:"Trevi Fountain",work:"La Dolce Vita",loc:"Rome, Italy",desc:"The scene in Fellini's La Dolce Vita where Anita Ekberg steps into the fountain is one of the great moments in film history.\nThe huge Baroque fountain sculptures and clear water suddenly appear among narrow Roman alleys and a square.\nAccording to legend, throwing a coin over your shoulder means you will return to Rome, so it is always crowded with tourists."},
64:{name:"Bocca della Verità",work:"Roman Holiday",loc:"Rome, Italy",desc:"This marble face sculpture in Rome is famous from the scene where Audrey Hepburn and Gregory Peck play with their hands in its mouth.\nIt stands at the entrance of the church of Santa Maria in Cosmedin, and legend says it bites off the hand of a liar.\nA line forms to put a hand in and take a photo like the scene in the film, but it is free."},
65:{name:"Petra Treasury (Al-Khazneh)",work:"Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade",loc:"Petra, Jordan",desc:"Al-Khazneh, which appears as the exterior of the temple housing the Holy Grail in Indiana Jones 3, is a Nabataean-era structure carved into rock.\nWalking through the narrow canyon called the \"Siq,\" a huge facade carved into a rose-colored cliff suddenly appears.\nIt is a UNESCO World Heritage site, and the \"Petra by Night\" event decorated with candles is popular."},
66:{name:"Millennium Bridge",work:"Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince",loc:"London, United Kingdom",desc:"This pedestrian-only bridge was the setting of the opening scene in Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince in which the Death Eaters destroy the bridge.\nA sleek steel suspension bridge over the Thames, it connects St Paul's Cathedral and Tate Modern.\nShortly after opening it earned the nickname \"the Wobbly Bridge\" for its swaying; it has since been reinforced and is safe to cross."},
67:{name:"Glen Etive",work:"Skyfall (007)",loc:"Scottish Highlands, United Kingdom",desc:"This is the lonely highland scenery that James Bond and M pass through on the way to the Skyfall estate in Skyfall.\nMisty mountains, a remote road, and the River Etive come together in a typical Scottish landscape.\nAfter the film's release it became a photo spot known as the \"Skyfall Road.\""},
68:{name:"Maya Bay",work:"The Beach",loc:"Phi Phi Islands, Thailand",desc:"Appearing as a paradise secret beach in DiCaprio's The Beach, it became a world-famous tourist spot.\nA white-sand beach spreads in an emerald bay surrounded by limestone cliffs.\nAfter tourist crowds damaged the coral, it was closed, and it has since reopened on a limited basis after a recovery period."},
69:{name:"Googleplex",work:"The Internship",loc:"Mountain View, California, USA",desc:"The setting of the comedy The Internship, in which Vince Vaughn and Owen Wilson work as interns, is the Google headquarters campus.\nColorful bicycles, slides, and free cafeterias show the free-spirited culture of Silicon Valley as it appears in the film.\nInterior access is restricted for the general public, but you can look around the visitor center and the garden of Android statues."},
70:{name:"Kastani Beach, Skopelos",work:"Mamma Mia!",loc:"Skopelos, Greece",desc:"This Greek island is where Sophie's wedding and dance scenes were filmed in the musical film Mamma Mia!.\nWhite-walled, blue-roofed churches, pine forests, and clear sea come together to show the charm of a Mediterranean resort.\nThe church of Agios Ioannis, where the wedding in the film takes place, stands on a rock on a hilltop and has become a tourist attraction."},
71:{name:"Rodeo Drive",work:"Pretty Woman",loc:"Beverly Hills, California, USA",desc:"This is the setting of the scene in Pretty Woman where Vivian shops along the street and experiences a rise in social status.\nA high-end shopping street where world-famous luxury brands gather, with palm trees and clean streets.\nEven without shopping, strolling the street and window shopping lets you feel the atmosphere of the film."},
72:{name:"Manawaiopuna Falls",work:"Jurassic Park",loc:"Kauai, Hawaii, USA",desc:"This waterfall was used in the scene in Jurassic Park where the helicopter descends toward the island and the characters first see the waterfall of the dinosaur island.\nIt lies on private land on the Hawaiian island of Kauai and can be seen only on helicopter tours.\nThe waterfall dropping between lush forest and cliffs conveys the mysterious first impression from the film exactly as it is."},
73:{name:"Hollywood Walk of Fame",work:"Once Upon a Time in Hollywood",loc:"Los Angeles, USA",desc:"Tarantino's film meticulously recreates 1969 Hollywood, and the Walk of Fame and theater marquees appear as backdrops.\nMore than 2,700 star-shaped markers on the sidewalk carry the names of actors, singers, and directors.\nSimply walking, along with the hand and footprints in front of the Chinese Theatre, lets you feel the history of the film industry."},
74:{name:"Monument Valley",work:"Forrest Gump",loc:"Utah / Arizona, USA",desc:"The scene where Forrest Gump stops his cross-country run was filmed on a road near here, which came to be called \"Forrest Gump Point.\"\nRed sandstone buttes rising from the desert are a symbol of the Western and have been used in many films.\nMany people take photos in the middle of the road, but you should be careful of traffic."},
75:{name:"Burj Khalifa",work:"Mission: Impossible – Ghost Protocol",loc:"Dubai, United Arab Emirates",desc:"The building in the famous scene where Tom Cruise climbs the exterior wall himself is the 828 m Burj Khalifa.\nThe tallest building in the world and a symbol of Dubai, its observation deck shows the desert and city at a glance.\nAt night fountain and LED light shows are held, offering a dazzling atmosphere different from the thrill of the film."},
76:{name:"Portobello Road",work:"Notting Hill",loc:"London, United Kingdom",desc:"The street and market scenes of the film Notting Hill, in which Hugh Grant plays a bookshop owner, were filmed here.\nThe street lined with pastel-colored houses and antique shops is especially lively when the Saturday market is held.\nThe blue door house and the bookshop from the film are real buildings and have become photo spots."},
77:{name:"Grafton Street",work:"Once",loc:"Dublin, Ireland",desc:"This is the busy Dublin street where the protagonist plays as a street performer in the musical film Once.\nA pedestrian-only street lined with buskers, flower stalls, and shops, it is always lively.\nCalled the holy ground of busking in Dublin, it is a good place to walk while recalling the mood of the film's hit song \"Falling Slowly.\""},
78:{name:"Golden Gate Bridge",work:"Rise of the Planet of the Apes",loc:"San Francisco, USA",desc:"The setting of the scene in Rise of the Planet of the Apes where a group of apes confront police on the bridge.\nThe vermilion suspension bridge blended with fog is known as a symbol of San Francisco.\nPopular routes include walking across the bridge or viewing it from the Marin Headlands and taking photos."},
79:{name:"Grand Canal, Venice",work:"Casino Royale (007)",loc:"Venice, Italy",desc:"In the ending of Casino Royale, a building sinks into the water in a Venice scene.\nPalaces and churches line the Grand Canal, where gondolas and water buses travel.\nSights seen in the film, such as the Rialto Bridge and the Salute church, continue throughout the city."},
80:{name:"Bodleian Library",work:"Harry Potter series",loc:"Oxford, United Kingdom",desc:"This Gothic building of the University of Oxford was used as the Hogwarts library and infirmary in the Harry Potter series.\nThe vaulted ceiling and elaborate carvings of the Divinity School create the atmosphere of the magic school in the films.\nYou can see the interior on a guided tour that also explains the film locations."},
81:{name:"Pont Neuf",work:"The Lovers on the Bridge",loc:"Paris, France",desc:"Leos Carax's film portrays the love of homeless lovers on the Pont Neuf bridge over the Seine in Paris.\nIts name means \"New Bridge,\" but completed in 1607 it is one of the oldest bridges in Paris.\nThe fireworks scene in the film is famous, and on the Seine riverside walk you can enjoy the view with the sunset."},
82:{name:"Bir-Hakeim Bridge",work:"Inception",loc:"Paris, France",desc:"This two-level bridge over the Seine is where the scene of Ariadne folding up the dream space in Inception was filmed.\nThe steel structure and stone pillars create a unique view near the Eiffel Tower in Paris.\nIt is a good spot for photos with the Eiffel Tower in the background, so many photographers and film fans visit."},
83:{name:"Philadelphia Museum of Art Steps",work:"Rocky",loc:"Philadelphia, USA",desc:"These are the stairs made famous by the scene where Rocky Balboa, after training, runs up them and raises both arms.\nFrom the top of the 72 steps you can see the whole of Philadelphia, and there is a Rocky statue at the bottom.\nMost visitors run up the stairs and strike a pose, making it a popular spot."},
84:{name:"Marina Bay Sands",work:"Crazy Rich Asians",loc:"Singapore",desc:"A skyscraper resort complex used in scenes of Crazy Rich Asians showing the glamorous world of Singapore's wealthy.\nA ship-shaped SkyPark sits atop three towers, with an infinity pool on the roof.\nAt night, light shows with Gardens by the Bay let you enjoy an atmosphere from the film."},
85:{name:"Unisphere",work:"Men in Black",loc:"Queens, New York, USA",desc:"A giant globe-shaped structure that appears as a spaceship in the first Men in Black film.\nBuilt for the 1964 New York World's Fair, it is a stainless-steel globe about 43 m in diameter.\nIt stands in Flushing Meadows Park, drawing film fans and photographers, and there are museums nearby."},
86:{name:"Shakespeare and Company",work:"Before Sunset",loc:"Paris, France",desc:"This English-language bookstore in Paris is where Jesse and Céline reunite after nine years in Before Sunset.\nAcross from Notre-Dame on the Seine, the bookstore is famous for its maze-like shelves, small rooms, and beds hidden among the books.\nIt has a literary tradition of writers such as Hemingway frequenting it, and author readings are still held."},
87:{name:"Manhattan Bridge View",work:"Once Upon a Time in America",loc:"Brooklyn, New York, USA",desc:"The composition on Sergio Leone's film poster, with the Manhattan Bridge seen between arched buildings, became famous.\nPeople try to shoot this composition on Washington Street in DUMBO all day long.\nA landmark of the New York cityscape, it is popular not only with film fans but also with ordinary travelers."},
88:{name:"Zhangjiajie National Forest Park",work:"Avatar",loc:"Zhangjiajie, Hunan, China",desc:"This sandstone pillar landscape in China is known as an inspiration for the \"Hallelujah Mountains\" design in Avatar.\nThousands of quartz sandstone pillars rising out of the mist are reminiscent of the floating mountains in the film.\nWith a glass bridge, cable cars, and trekking trails, it is a tourist spot that film fans visit and marvel at."},
89:{name:"Niagara Falls",work:"Superman II",loc:"Canada–USA border",desc:"This is where the scene in Superman II of Superman saving a falling boy in front of the falls was filmed.\nStraddling the border between Canada and the United States, the falls pour down tens of millions of liters of water per minute.\nThe \"Maid of the Mist\" boat ride that takes you close to the falls is the signature tourist course."},
90:{name:"Casino de Monte-Carlo",work:"Iron Man 2",loc:"Monte Carlo, Monaco",desc:"The scene in Iron Man 2 where Tony Stark meets trouble during the Monaco Grand Prix was filmed around this area.\nThe splendid 19th-century casino building and square show the atmosphere of a wealthy resort.\nDuring the annual Monaco Grand Prix it becomes part of the circuit and the whole city is swept up in a festival mood."},
91:{name:"Ohio State Reformatory",work:"The Shawshank Redemption",loc:"Mansfield, Ohio, USA",desc:"This former prison used as the filming location for The Shawshank Redemption appears as Shawshank Prison with its Gothic building and tall iron cell blocks.\nThe building closed in 1990 and now operates as a museum, and film location tours are popular.\nYou can see spaces from the film in person, such as the warden's office where Andy stood and the library."},
92:{name:"Park Hyatt Tokyo",work:"Lost in Translation",loc:"Shinjuku, Tokyo, Japan",desc:"The hotel where Bob and Charlotte share their loneliness in Sofia Coppola's film is the Park Hyatt Tokyo.\nLocated on the 41st floor and above of a Shinjuku skyscraper, the New York Bar and restaurant with sweeping Tokyo night views create the atmosphere of the film.\nAfter the film's release it became a pilgrimage site for fans around the world, and you can recall scenes from the film while drinking whisky at the hotel bar."},
93:{name:"Castel Sant'Angelo",work:"Angels & Demons",loc:"Rome, Italy",desc:"It appears as the key location to the Illuminati's secret passage in the film Angels & Demons, based on Dan Brown's novel.\nA circular building originally built as a tomb for the Roman emperor Hadrian and later used as a papal fortress and prison.\nThe secret passage \"Passetto di Borgo,\" leading from the Vatican, actually exists, lending reality to the film's premise."},
94:{name:"Chungking Mansions",work:"Chungking Express",loc:"Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong",desc:"The complex that serves as the setting of the first episode of Wong Kar-wai's Chungking Express is Chungking Mansions.\nNarrow corridors, currency exchange shops, and Indian and African restaurants show Hong Kong's crowded, multicultural scenery.\nThe film's lonely yet sensuous mood blends with the neon-lit streets of Tsim Sha Tsui and is loved by fans."},
95:{name:"Statue of Liberty",work:"Planet of the Apes (1968)",loc:"New York, USA",desc:"In the shocking final scene of the 1968 Planet of the Apes, the protagonist Taylor discovers the Statue of Liberty half-buried on a beach.\nThis copper statue, a gift from France to the United States, stands about 93 m tall including the pedestal and is a symbol of New York Harbor.\nYou can take a ferry to Liberty Island and climb up to the crown observation deck."},
96:{name:"Matterhorn",work:"Paramount opening logo",loc:"Zermatt, Switzerland",desc:"This iconic Alpine peak is known as the model for the mountain in the Paramount Pictures opening logo.\nIts pyramid-shaped summit at 4,478 m rises on the border between Switzerland and Italy.\nTaking the Gornergrat train up from the village of Zermatt lets you see the Matterhorn and its reflection in a lake."},
97:{name:"Tongariro National Park",work:"The Lord of the Rings",loc:"North Island, New Zealand",desc:"This volcanic national park was used as a filming location for Mordor and Mount Doom in The Lord of the Rings.\nMount Ngauruhoe appears as Mount Doom, and the area around Mount Ruapehu appears as the wasteland of Mordor.\nThe Tongariro Alpine Crossing, a day-long trek, is popular as a way to walk through the film's scenery in person."},
98:{name:"Skellig Michael",work:"Star Wars: The Force Awakens",loc:"Kerry, Ireland",desc:"It appeared as the remote island where Luke Skywalker lived in hiding in Star Wars Episodes VII and VIII.\nA rocky island rising in the middle of the Atlantic, it is a UNESCO World Heritage site with beehive-shaped stone huts of a 6th–8th-century monastery.\nVisitor numbers are strictly limited, so the period and number of people who can go by boat are limited."},
99:{name:"Tikal",work:"Star Wars: A New Hope",loc:"Petén, Guatemala",desc:"These Maya ruins were the filming location for the rebel base \"Yavin 4\" in Star Wars: A New Hope.\nSunrise from the top of a pyramid temple rising above the jungle calls to mind the scenery from the film.\nIt is a UNESCO World Heritage site, and tours that enter at dawn to see the misty jungle are popular."},
100:{name:"Sassi di Matera",work:"No Time to Die (007)",loc:"Basilicata, Italy",desc:"This city was used as a filming location for the opening chase of No Time to Die and for Mel Gibson's The Passion of the Christ.\nThe limestone cave dwellings called \"Sassi\" spread in layers along the ravine and have preserved thousands of years of history.\nA UNESCO World Heritage site and 2019 European Capital of Culture, it is visited by film fans and history lovers alike."},
101:{name:"Eilean Donan Castle",work:"Highlander",loc:"Scotland, United Kingdom",desc:"This castle on a Scottish loch appears as the MacLeod clan castle in the 1986 film Highlander.\nStanding on an island where three sea lochs meet, it looks magical blended with the mist.\nConnected by a stone bridge, the castle lies on the way to the Isle of Skye and is famous as a photo spot."},
102:{name:"Alnwick Castle",work:"Harry Potter series",loc:"Northumberland, United Kingdom",desc:"This medieval castle was filmed as the exterior of Hogwarts and the broomstick lesson scenes in Harry Potter films 1 and 2.\nIt is the home of the Duke of Northumberland and is still open to the public.\nBroomstick-flying experiences and film location tours are available, drawing fans."},
103:{name:"Glenfinnan Viaduct",work:"Harry Potter series",loc:"Scottish Highlands, United Kingdom",desc:"This curved railway bridge appears in the scene of the Hogwarts Express carrying Harry past.\nThe viaduct, made of 21 arches and completed in 1898, crosses the mountainous terrain of western Scotland.\nIf you visit at the time the steam train \"Jacobite\" passes, you can see the scene from the film just as it is."},
104:{name:"Cliffs of Moher",work:"Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince",loc:"County Clare, Ireland",desc:"It was used as the setting for the scene in Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince where Dumbledore and Harry head to the cave.\nExtending about 8 km along the Atlantic, the cliffs reach up to 214 m, with powerful waves and mist.\nIt also appears in other films such as The Princess Bride and is loved by film fans."},
105:{name:"Mount Rushmore",work:"North by Northwest",loc:"South Dakota, USA",desc:"The climactic scene in Hitchcock's North by Northwest, in which the protagonist is chased on the presidential faces, is famous.\nThe faces of George Washington, Thomas Jefferson, Theodore Roosevelt, and Abraham Lincoln are carved into the granite mountain.\nThe scene in the film was not shot on location but used sets and compositing."},
106:{name:"Hoover Dam",work:"Transformers",loc:"Nevada / Arizona, USA",desc:"The fight between the Autobots and Decepticons in the first Transformers film was filmed here.\nAn arch-gravity dam built on the Colorado River and completed in 1936, it supplies electricity and water.\nAt the visitor center you can take a tour of the inside of the dam and use the observation deck."},
107:{name:"Alcatraz Island",work:"The Rock",loc:"San Francisco, USA",desc:"The former federal prison that served as the main setting of The Rock, starring Sean Connery and Nicolas Cage.\nAn island in the middle of San Francisco Bay, it was notorious as an inescapable prison.\nTake a ferry in and tour the cells, yard, and lighthouse with an audio tour."},
108:{name:"Ta Prohm Temple",work:"Tomb Raider",loc:"Siem Reap, Cambodia",desc:"This is the filming location for the scenes of Lara Croft exploring a mysterious temple in Tomb Raider starring Angelina Jolie.\nAmong the Angkor ruins it is famous for huge tree roots wrapped around the temple walls.\nIt is a UNESCO World Heritage site, and visiting around sunrise lets you enjoy the quiet temple scenery."},
109:{name:"Iguazu Falls",work:"The Mission",loc:"Argentina–Brazil border",desc:"Scenes depicting the story of Jesuit missionaries in the 1986 film The Mission were filmed around Iguazu Falls.\n275 waterfalls form a semicircle, and the \"Devil's Throat\" is the largest drop.\nYou can see the falls from different viewpoints on the Brazilian and Argentine sides."},
110:{name:"Arashiyama Bamboo Grove",work:"Memoirs of a Geisha",loc:"Kyoto, Kyoto, Japan",desc:"A Kyoto landmark known as the inspiration for the bamboo path scene where Chiyo walks in Memoirs of a Geisha.\nBamboo tens of meters tall blocks the sky above the path, and the sound of wind creates a mysterious atmosphere.\nIt is often visited as a walking course together with nearby Togetsukyo Bridge and Tenryu-ji Temple."},
111:{name:"Dettifoss",work:"Prometheus",loc:"Northeast Iceland",desc:"This is where the scene in the opening of Ridley Scott's Prometheus, in which an alien throws himself in front of a waterfall, was filmed.\nOne of the waterfalls with the largest flow in Europe, its brown glacial water rushes down fiercely.\nThe desolate lava plateau and the roar of the waterfall create the film's alien atmosphere."},
112:{name:"Salar de Uyuni",work:"Star Wars: The Last Jedi",loc:"Potosí, Bolivia",desc:"The battle scenes on the salt planet \"Crait\" in The Last Jedi took inspiration from here.\nIn the rainy season a thin layer of water collects and shows a mirror-like landscape reflecting the sky.\nThe world's largest salt flat, it offers tour vehicles to photo spots and salt hotels."},
113:{name:"Svínafellsjökull Glacier",work:"Interstellar",loc:"Southeast Iceland",desc:"The scenes where Cooper's crew arrives on the ice planet in Interstellar were filmed around here.\nA glacier tongue belonging to Vatnajökull National Park, it combines blue ice with black volcanic ash.\nGuided tours with safety gear allow glacier hiking and ice cave exploration."},
114:{name:"Times Square",work:"I Am Legend",loc:"New York, USA",desc:"This is the setting of the scene where Will Smith drives a car through an empty New York square hunting deer in I Am Legend.\nNormally filled with dazzling billboards and crowds, the empty scene in the film felt all the more shocking.\nNeon lights as bright as day even at night are a symbol of New York, attracting tens of millions of tourists a year."},
115:{name:"Wiener Riesenrad",work:"The Third Man",loc:"Vienna, Austria",desc:"The setting of the great scene in the 1949 classic The Third Man in which Harry Lime and Holly Martins talk inside the Ferris wheel.\nBuilt in 1897 in Prater Park, it is one of the symbols of Vienna.\nRiding up in a red car shows all of Vienna and calls to mind lines from the film."},
116:{name:"Mirabell Gardens",work:"The Sound of Music",loc:"Salzburg, Austria",desc:"The garden where Maria and the children run around in the \"Do-Re-Mi\" scene in The Sound of Music.\nA Baroque palace, symmetrical flower gardens, and the Pegasus fountain make it beautiful in every season.\nThe composition with Hohensalzburg Fortress seen behind the garden is a famous photo point."},
117:{name:"Katz's Delicatessen",work:"When Harry Met Sally",loc:"New York, USA",desc:"The famous New York deli where the scene of Sally faking an orgasm in the middle of a restaurant in When Harry Met Sally was filmed.\nOpened in 1888 and famous for its pastrami sandwiches, it has a sign on the table from the film.\nIt is a landmark where not only film fans but also travelers looking for New York eateries wait in line to eat."},
118:{name:"Plaza de España, Seville",work:"Star Wars: Attack of the Clones",loc:"Seville, Spain",desc:"The palace interior and square scenes of the planet Naboo in Star Wars Episode II were filmed here.\nThe semicircular building, canal, and tile-decorated bridges were built for the 1929 exposition.\nTaking a small boat around the canal, you can enjoy architectural beauty similar to scenes in the film."},
119:{name:"Busan Station",work:"Train to Busan",loc:"Busan, South Korea",desc:"In Yeon Sang-ho's zombie film Train to Busan, the city where the train heads for its final destination is Busan, and Busan Station is the setting of the climax.\nMost actual filming took place in Daegu, Daejeon, and elsewhere, but because of the film's title and ending, Busan Station has become a symbolic place.\nIn the square in front of the station, tourists who arrive on the KTX take photos while recalling the film."},
120:{name:"Han River, Yeouido",work:"The Host",loc:"Seoul, South Korea",desc:"The scene in Bong Joon-ho's The Host where the monster first appears on the Han River bank was filmed around Yeouido.\nThe Han River Park is a place where Seoul citizens relax in daily life, which made the peaceful scenery in the film all the more contrasting.\nRiver cruises, bicycle paths, and night views are popular, making it a fresh experience to visit after watching the film."},
121:{name:"Bridge over the River Kwai",work:"The Bridge on the River Kwai",loc:"Kanchanaburi, Thailand",desc:"Near the actual railway bridge that was the setting of the film about a World War II prisoner camp.\nThe film was shot in Sri Lanka, but the bridge in Kanchanaburi symbolizes the history of the construction of the Burma Railway.\nAt the nearby museum and war cemetery you can reflect on the sacrifices of the prisoners and workers of that time."},
122:{name:"Otaru Canal",work:"Love Letter",loc:"Otaru, Hokkaido, Japan",desc:"In Shunji Iwai's film Love Letter, the snow-covered streets of Otaru appear as a setting that overlaps with the protagonist's memories.\nThe canal lined with red-brick warehouses and gas lamps is romantic in winter when snow and lights come together.\nAt the annual winter \"Otaru Snow Light Path\" event, candles are lit along the canal."}
};
